// MsgResetDemocraticAllocations clears every democratic vote, so the emission
// stream is only directed by humans who show up and vote again.
//
// Votes are cast once and then persist indefinitely, so over time the split
// reflects whoever was active when they last voted rather than who is active
// now. This retires the whole slate at once.
//
// It does not touch registrations: nobody loses their verified-human status or
// has to re-prove personhood, they only have to re-express a preference. Options
// survive too, along with any ERTH they have already accrued, so no recipient
// loses a claimable balance and nobody re-pays the address-option fee. Until
// voters return, the stream simply accrues to nothing.
